#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064073 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4851cda0-b113-5476-8e09-cceada5f07f6" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Number"}] :question/id #uuid "cecc0a5a-10be-59b9-a8c5-ae907679ed65" :question/math-academy-id "e-4474" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $2+ (-6)$." :question/worked-solution "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give\n\n$$\n2+ (-6) = 2-6\n$$\n\nThen, we move $6$ spaces to the left of $2$ on a number line.\n\n![](images/ed/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nWe end up at $-4$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n2 + (-6) = -4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "498454ca-7ef2-57fb-aa4b-4884aed0c24e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Decimal"}] :question/id #uuid "f5138ecd-8e2e-5f83-a286-d770a53fba6f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4478" :question/problem "What is the value of $-1 + (-2.5)$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n-1 + (-2.5) = -1 - 2.5\n$$\n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n\n$$\n-1 - 2.5 = -3.5\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd8feed5-e1ee-5d1a-bba3-4fb2adee27ed" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "aa932148-f7fc-5e12-ad35-e9e90df25cc6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4484" :question/problem "Find the value of $-\\dfrac{2}{5} + \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{10}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac 2 5 + \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{10}\\right) = -\\dfrac 2 5 -\\dfrac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to convert the fractions to have the same denominator. To convert\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nto have a denominator of $10$, we multiply the numerator and denominator by $2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{2}{5} =-\\dfrac{2 \\times 2}{5 \\times 2} =-\\dfrac{4}{10}\n$$\n\nNow, the subtraction problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac{2}{5} - \\frac{3}{10} &= -\\frac{4}{10} - \\frac{3}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the two fractions now have the same denominator, we can combine the numerators:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{10} - \\frac{3}{10} = \\frac{-4 - 3}{10}\n$$\n\nNext, we work out $-4 - 3$ using our number line.\n\n![](images/dd/dd96e6f3b2a3e35d0f792cb828ef905cfb0ea86b0962b017ceaa0630e4aba144.png)\n\nWe find that $-4-3=-7$. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-4 - 3} {10} = \\dfrac{-7}{10} = -\\dfrac{7}{10}\n$$"}]}
